Tom Wilson wrote:

>Everyone talks about how he finished, how he died, or how to progress past
>______, so here's something different. I'm curious if others start nethack
>the way I do. Having completed older versions of the game before, I tend to
>throw caution to the wind at the beginning. I drink most potions, read most
>scrolls and books, and zap most wands -- without identifying them. I typically
>fight monsters without watching to see how close to death I am. If I make it
>to the mines, I start to be a little more cautious. Usually, at this point, I
>have already identified several items and know what my chances are on new
>ones.
>
>How do you start?

Well, since I always play Tourists these days, I have to be a bit more careful.
I tend to move as slowly as my patience will allow, retreating to safe corners
to recover HPs, getting my pet in on monster-whacking action, that sort of
thing.  I eat any eggs I'm carrying so they won't spoil, save the scrolls of
magic mapping in case I get pretty far, identify gems and wands as soon as
possible (by chest-kicking and engraving, respectively) and read or quaff
indiscriminately.  Weapons and armor I always have my pet check before I use
it.  Oh, and I don't do the mines until I have a decent hit level and AC.

Of course, sometimes I rush headlong into danger, or forget to use other
resources (like memorized spells) when the hit points get low.  Lazuli-T
usually pays for such brashness, though.  Wierd thing is, I've had my best
games with tourists (at least since 3.0...)

